{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Security Checker",
  "description": "Scan for common security vulnerabilities and sensitive data exposure",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "**/*.dart",
      "**/*.ts"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "🔒 Security Scan:\n\n**SENSITIVE DATA EXPOSURE:**\n❌ Hardcoded API keys, tokens, passwords\n❌ Credentials in code\n❌ Private keys or certificates\n❌ Database connection strings\n❌ Email addresses or phone numbers\n\n**FLUTTER SPECIFIC:**\n❌ Storing tokens in SharedPreferences (use FlutterSecureStorage)\n❌ Logging sensitive data\n❌ Exposing user data in error messages\n❌ Missing input validation\n❌ SQL injection risks (raw queries)\n\n**NESTJS SPECIFIC:**\n❌ Missing authentication guards\n❌ Exposing internal errors to client\n❌ No rate limiting\n❌ Missing input validation\n❌ SQL injection (raw queries)\n❌ XSS vulnerabilities\n❌ Missing CORS configuration\n\n**PROPER PATTERNS:**\n✅ Use environment variables (.env)\n✅ Use FlutterSecureStorage for tokens\n✅ Validate all user inputs\n✅ Use parameterized queries\n✅ Sanitize error messages\n✅ Implement rate limiting\n✅ Use authentication guards\n\n**CHECK FOR:**\n- Regex patterns for API keys, tokens\n- Hardcoded credentials\n- Insecure storage usage\n- Missing validation decorators\n- Raw SQL queries\n- Exposed stack traces\n\nIf security issues found, report with CRITICAL severity and suggest immediate fixes."
  }
}
